WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.819 --> 00:00:15.441
Hamlet thought about what to do next as he watched musicians gathering in the great hall.

2
00:00:16.042 --> 00:00:18.663
Soon Rosencrantz and Guildenstern returned.

3
00:00:18.683 --> 00:00:24.786
"Sir," said Guildenstern to Hamlet, "the king is angry and your mother is very upset."

4
00:00:24.806 --> 00:00:30.148
"Perhaps you'd feel better," added Rosencrantz, "if you told us what's troubling you."

5
00:00:31.124 --> 00:00:33.925
Hamlet was certain now that his friends were spying on him.

6
00:00:34.865 --> 00:00:36.786
He grabbed a flute from one of the musicians.

7
00:00:36.806 --> 00:00:38.666
"Can you play this?"

8
00:00:39.146 --> 00:00:39.506
he said.

9
00:00:40.687 --> 00:00:44.268
"I cannot get a sound out of it," replied Guildenstern nervously.

10
00:00:44.288 --> 00:00:49.529
"And yet you think that you can get sounds out of me—that I'll tell you what's on my

11
00:00:49.589 --> 00:00:51.290
mind!" exclaimed Hamlet.

12
00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:55.351
"You are wrong to think I am easier to play than a flute!"

13
00:00:56.371 --> 00:00:59.952
Rosencrantz and Guildenstern scurried out just as Polonius entered.

14
00:01:01.236 --> 00:01:04.077
"Your mother wishes to see you, my lord," the old man said.

15
00:01:04.977 --> 00:01:07.298
Then Polonius went to Gertrude's sitting room.

16
00:01:07.318 --> 00:01:14.220
"When Hamlet gets here, try to find out what's really bothering him," he instructed and hid himself behind

17
00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:14.940
a heavy curtain.

18
00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:19.261
Meanwhile Rosencrantz and Guildenstern had gone straight to the king.

19
00:01:20.201 --> 00:01:23.582
They reported that Hamlet seemed even more deranged than before.

20
00:01:24.202 --> 00:01:26.363
When they left, the king was all alone.

21
00:01:26.383 --> 00:01:28.784
"What have I done?"

22
00:01:29.364 --> 00:01:29.764
he thought.

23
00:01:30.268 --> 00:01:33.771
"My sin is the greatest of all—I've killed my own brother.

24
00:01:34.812 --> 00:01:39.376
How can I be forgiven, since I am not willing to give up what I have gained by

25
00:01:39.396 --> 00:01:42.018
my foul deed—my brother's kingdom and his queen?

26
00:01:43.179 --> 00:01:47.402
Angels in heaven, soften this heart of steel and help me repent!"

27
00:01:47.943 --> 00:01:50.044
He knelt down and tried to pray.

28
00:01:51.005 --> 00:01:55.669
At that moment Hamlet walked past Claudius' chambers and saw the king kneeling.

29
00:01:55.689 --> 00:01:58.992
"I could kill him now so easily!"

30
00:01:59.232 --> 00:02:00.593
he thought, drawing his sword.

31
00:02:02.054 --> 00:02:02.895
Then he paused.

32
00:02:02.915 --> 00:02:09.219
"Claudius murdered my father before my father had time to confess his sins, so he could not go

33
00:02:09.299 --> 00:02:10.079
straight to heaven.

34
00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:16.404
But if I kill Claudius now, while he's praying, this murderer will go to heaven!

35
00:02:16.864 --> 00:02:18.065
What kind of revenge is that?

36
00:02:19.045 --> 00:02:24.549
It's better to kill him when he's drinking or gambling—when his soul is black and headed straight to

37
00:02:24.609 --> 00:02:28.852
hell!" Putting his sword back in its sheath, Hamlet quietly left.

38
00:02:29.856 --> 00:02:31.377
Claudius sighed and stood up.

39
00:02:32.238 --> 00:02:35.240
"My words are empty," he muttered.

40
00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:37.701
"My heart is not in them.

41
00:02:38.262 --> 00:02:40.903
And empty words can never reach God's ear."

42
00:02:41.844 --> 00:02:46.947
When Hamlet got to the queen's chambers, Gertrude said, "You have offended the king, your father."

43
00:02:47.888 --> 00:02:52.591
"Mother," replied Hamlet, "you have offended the king, my father."

44
00:02:53.592 --> 00:02:55.213
"How dare you speak to me this way?"

45
00:02:56.174 --> 00:02:59.516
Gertrude began to get up from her chair, but Hamlet pushed her back down.

46
00:03:00.884 --> 00:03:03.105
"You shall not budge until we talk this out!"

47
00:03:03.545 --> 00:03:04.005
he shouted.

48
00:03:04.986 --> 00:03:08.707
Frightened by Hamlet's roughness, the queen cried out, "Do you mean to kill me?

49
00:03:09.208 --> 00:03:14.310
Help!" Polonius, who could hear but not see what was happening, panicked.

50
00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:15.690
"Help, help!"

51
00:03:16.231 --> 00:03:16.671
he yelled.

52
00:03:17.671 --> 00:03:24.334
Hamlet, thinking that Polonius was Claudius, thrust his sword through the curtain and stabbed the old man.

53
00:03:25.294 --> 00:03:26.195
Gertrude gasped.

54
00:03:26.755 --> 00:03:28.776
"What a rash and bloody deed!"

55
00:03:29.832 --> 00:03:33.293
"Almost as bloody as killing a king and marrying his brother!"

56
00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:34.113
said Hamlet.

57
00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:35.934
"Killing a king?"

58
00:03:36.514 --> 00:03:38.015
echoed Gertrude, bewildered.

59
00:03:38.975 --> 00:03:41.756
Hamlet lifted the curtain and saw Polonius' body.

60
00:03:41.776 --> 00:03:45.037
"Farewell, you old, meddling fool.

61
00:03:45.997 --> 00:03:48.798
Being a busybody can be dangerous," he said.

62
00:03:48.818 --> 00:03:51.059
"Now, Mother.

63
00:03:51.479 --> 00:03:59.811
My father was handsome, noble, kind—how could you dishonor his memory by so hastily marrying that villain and

64
00:03:59.931 --> 00:04:02.472
murderer?" The queen went pale.

65
00:04:02.492 --> 00:04:04.354
"Oh Hamlet, stop!"

66
00:04:05.374 --> 00:04:07.936
At that moment the ghost appeared to the prince.

67
00:04:08.456 --> 00:04:09.897
Hamlet jumped up, staring.

68
00:04:09.917 --> 00:04:11.578
"What do you want?

69
00:04:12.038 --> 00:04:14.079
Do you come to scold me for taking too long?"

70
00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:18.101
"You must avenge me," wailed the ghost.

71
00:04:19.162 --> 00:04:20.943
"Who are you speaking to?"

72
00:04:21.483 --> 00:04:22.244
Gertrude whispered.

73
00:04:23.156 --> 00:04:24.016
"My father's spirit!

74
00:04:24.237 --> 00:04:24.917
Can't you see it?"

75
00:04:25.897 --> 00:04:28.578
"Alas, you are truly mad!"

76
00:04:29.179 --> 00:04:29.939
his mother moaned.

77
00:04:30.899 --> 00:04:34.301
The ghost vanished, and Hamlet looked down at the dead Polonius.

78
00:04:34.321 --> 00:04:37.362
"For this I am sorry," he muttered.

79
00:04:37.822 --> 00:04:38.983
"Mother, good night."

80
00:04:40.403 --> 00:04:46.266
After Hamlet left, Gertrude rushed to Claudius and told him that Hamlet had killed Polonius in a fit

81
00:04:46.346 --> 00:04:46.966
of madness.

82
00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:50.688
The king was now very afraid for his own life.

83
00:04:51.252 --> 00:04:53.533
He summoned Rosencrantz and Guildenstern.

84
00:04:54.493 --> 00:04:57.355
"Hamlet has committed a grave crime," said the king.

85
00:04:57.375 --> 00:04:59.836
"You must take him to England.

86
00:05:00.296 --> 00:05:01.636
There is a boat leaving soon."

87
00:05:02.637 --> 00:05:04.398
He handed Rosencrantz a letter.

88
00:05:04.418 --> 00:05:07.839
"Present this to the king of England on your arrival."

89
00:05:08.799 --> 00:05:14.022
What no one but the king knew was that the letter contained orders to have Hamlet put to

90
00:05:14.082 --> 00:05:19.564
death! That night Rosencrantz, Guildenstern, and Hamlet rode toward the coast.

91
00:05:20.648 --> 00:05:24.171
On their way they saw thousands of soldiers marching along the road.

92
00:05:25.112 --> 00:05:27.894
Hamlet stopped their captain and inquired who they were.

93
00:05:27.914 --> 00:05:31.798
"We are the army of Norway, sir," replied the captain.

94
00:05:31.818 --> 00:05:37.142
"Your king gave us permission to march through Denmark on our way to Poland."

95
00:05:37.162 --> 00:05:41.125
"Prince Fortinbras is waging war against Poland?"

96
00:05:41.526 --> 00:05:41.986
said Hamlet.

97
00:05:42.967 --> 00:05:44.749
"Not really," answered the captain.

98
00:05:44.769 --> 00:05:50.817
"He wants to capture only a tiny piece of land, which the Poles will fight to defend."

99
00:05:51.798 --> 00:05:52.998
Hamlet was astonished.

100
00:05:53.639 --> 00:06:00.162
"Fortinbras has put together a whole army," he thought, "and will risk his life for a small patch

101
00:06:00.222 --> 00:06:00.663
of earth.

102
00:06:01.903 --> 00:06:05.445
I have a beloved father's murder to avenge, and I've done nothing!

103
00:06:06.026 --> 00:06:07.446
Fortinbras shames me!"

104
00:06:08.547 --> 00:06:11.569
At that moment something changed inside Hamlet.

105
00:06:12.509 --> 00:06:16.972
He resolved to find a way to return to Elsinore and kill Claudius.

106
00:06:18.072 --> 00:06:24.016
"From this time forth," he said to himself, "my thoughts will be either bloody or worthless!"

107
00:06:25.057 --> 00:06:30.740
But for now, with Rosencrantz and Guildenstern as guards, he had no choice but to ride on toward

108
00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:31.141
the ship.

109
00:06:32.502 --> 00:06:35.143
Back at Elsinore, another tragedy was unfolding.

110
00:06:35.744 --> 00:06:39.106
After the death of her father, Ophelia had gone insane.

111
00:06:40.167 --> 00:06:43.889
She wandered past Claudius and Gertrude, who were seated in the great hall.

112
00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:51.614
She was carrying wildflowers, speaking nonsense, and singing bits of sad songs about love and death.

113
00:06:51.634 --> 00:06:55.955
"Grief has made her mad," said Gertrude sadly.

114
00:06:55.975 --> 00:07:02.378
"When sorrows come, they come not as single spies, but in battalions," replied Claudius.

115
00:07:03.399 --> 00:07:08.161
"Hamlet, the man she loved, has murdered her father, and now Hamlet is gone too."

116
00:07:09.141 --> 00:07:11.222
Suddenly they heard footsteps and shouts.

117
00:07:12.303 --> 00:07:15.444
A servant ran into the hall, quickly shutting the doors behind him.

118
00:07:16.456 --> 00:07:19.779
"Laertes has learned of his father's death and returned from France!"

119
00:07:20.159 --> 00:07:20.560
he cried.

120
00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:24.623
"The mob calls him ‘lord' and wants to crown him king!"

121
00:07:25.684 --> 00:07:28.866
The doors flew open as Laertes and his followers burst in.

122
00:07:30.268 --> 00:07:31.769
Laertes ran up to Claudius.

123
00:07:31.789 --> 00:07:35.412
"I want revenge on the man who killed my father!"

124
00:07:35.692 --> 00:07:36.152
he shouted.

125
00:07:36.172 --> 00:07:42.017
"Good Laertes, I am guiltless of your father's death," protested Claudius.

126
00:07:43.058 --> 00:07:47.134
Then Laertes walked up to Ophelia, but she did not recognize her brother.

127
00:07:48.094 --> 00:07:50.176
Instead she handed him some flowers.

128
00:07:51.257 --> 00:07:52.418
"Here," she said.

129
00:07:52.438 --> 00:07:53.739
"These are pansies.

130
00:07:54.279 --> 00:07:57.322
I wanted violets, but they withered when my father died.

131
00:07:57.842 --> 00:07:58.843
Now you must sing!"

132
00:07:59.844 --> 00:08:01.405
Laertes saw that she was mad.

133
00:08:01.425 --> 00:08:03.567
"Oh, sweet Ophelia!

134
00:08:03.847 --> 00:08:05.408
God in heaven, do you see this?"

135
00:08:05.949 --> 00:08:06.349
he cried.

136
00:08:06.369 --> 00:08:09.192
"I share your grief," said the king.

137
00:08:09.212 --> 00:08:12.594
"I swear your father's death will be avenged!"

138
00:08:13.615 --> 00:08:17.317
Not long after, a man came to see Horatio with a letter from Hamlet.

139
00:08:18.217 --> 00:08:21.598
The letter explained that Hamlet's ship had been attacked by pirates.

140
00:08:22.639 --> 00:08:28.081
But Hamlet had convinced the pirates to release him, and now he wanted Horatio to meet with him.

141
00:08:28.621 --> 00:08:31.022
Hamlet was on his way back to Elsinore!
